22081:
Open pipe fundamental is f_o = \frac{v}{2L_o}
Closed pipe odd harmonics are f_n = \frac{nv}{4L_c} with n = 1, 3, 5
Third harmonic means n = 3 so f_c = \frac{3v}{4L_c} with L_c = 20\text{ cm}
Equating f_o = f_c gives L_o = \frac{2L_c}{3} = \frac{40}{3}\text{ cm}
This is about 13.3\text{ cm}, matching 13.2\text{ cm} → (C)

22082:
Escape needs v_{rms} = v_e with v_e = 11.2 \times 10^{3}\text{ m s}^{-1}
Kinetic form is \sqrt{\frac{3k_BT}{m}} = v_e so T = \frac{mv_e^{2}}{3k_B}
Insert m = 2.76 \times 10^{-26}\text{ kg} and k_B = 1.38 \times 10^{-23}\text{ J K}^{-1}
Numerator is about 3.46 \times 10^{-18} and denominator is 4.14 \times 10^{-23}
Ratio gives T \approx 8.36 \times 10^{4}\text{ K} → (B)

22083:
Efficiency of ideal engine is \eta = 1 - \frac{T_c}{T_h}
Freezing point is T_c = 273\text{ K} and boiling point is T_h = 373\text{ K}
Hence \eta = 1 - \frac{273}{373} = \frac{100}{373}
Computation gives \eta \approx 0.268 = 26.8\%
This matches option C
→ (C)

22085:
Series current is I = \frac{E}{R + R} for one cell with total resistance 2R
Parallel of n cells gives emf E with internal resistance \frac{R}{n}
Parallel current is 10I = \frac{E}{R/n + R}
Solving gives n = 10
This matches option C
→ (C)

22088:
Angular fringe width is \theta = \frac{\lambda}{d}
With \lambda and D fixed, width scales inversely with slit separation d
New separation scales as d^{\prime} = d \times \frac{0.20}{0.21} adjusted for the listed settings
Computation gives d^{\prime} = 1.9\text{ mm}
This matches option B
→ (B)

22091:
Electron in field \vec{E} = -E_0\hat{i} feels force -e\vec{E} along +x, accelerating it
Speed grows as v(t) = v_0 + \frac{eE_0t}{m}
De Broglie wavelength \lambda = \frac{h}{mv} therefore falls as \lambda(t) = \frac{\lambda_0}{1 + eE_0t/mv_0}
This matches option C
→ (C)

22094:
Base loop gives I_B = \frac{V_i - V_{BE}}{R_B} with the listed resistor values
Substitution gives I_B = 40\text{ }\mu\text{A}
Collector loop gives I_C = 5\text{ mA}
Current gain is \beta = \frac{I_C}{I_B} = 125
This matches option D
