22100:
Stored magnetic energy is U = \frac{1}{2}LI^{2}
Rearranged form is L = \frac{2U}{I^{2}}
Insert U = 25 \times 10^{-3}\text{ J} and I = 60 \times 10^{-3}\text{ A}
Denominator is 3600 \times 10^{-6} so L = \frac{50 \times 10^{-3}}{3600 \times 10^{-6}}
Evaluation gives L \approx 13.89\text{ H} → (D)

22103:
Successive closed-pipe resonances differ by half a wavelength
Separation is 73\text{ cm} - 20\text{ cm} = 53\text{ cm} so \frac{\lambda}{2} = 0.53\text{ m}
Hence \lambda = 1.06\text{ m} for fork frequency f = 320\text{ Hz}
Speed follows v = f\lambda = 320 \times 1.06
Product is about 339\text{ m/s} → (B)

22104:
SHM acceleration obeys a = \omega^{2}x in magnitude
Given a = 20\text{ m/s}^{2} at x = 5\text{ m} gives \omega^{2} = \frac{20}{5} = 4
Hence angular frequency is \omega = 2\text{ rad/s}
Period is T = \frac{2\pi}{\omega}
Substitution gives T = \pi\text{ s} → (B)

22107:
Average power is P = I_{rms}^{2}R with I_{rms} = \frac{V_{rms}}{Z}
Source gives V_{rms} = \frac{10}{\sqrt{2}}\text{ V} near 7.07\text{ V}
Reactances are X_L = 314 \times 0.02 = 6.28\text{ }\Omega and X_C = \frac{1}{314 \times 100 \times 10^{-6}} near 31.85\text{ }\Omega
Impedance is Z = \sqrt{R^{2} + (X_L - X_C)^{2}} with R = 50\text{ }\Omega
Result is P \approx 0.79\text{ W} → (C)

22108:
Current sensitivity is S_I = \frac{\phi}{I} and voltage sensitivity is S_V = \frac{\phi}{V}
Ratio cancels deflection as \frac{S_I}{S_V} = \frac{V}{I} = R
Given S_I = 5\text{ div/mA} = 5000\text{ div/A} and S_V = 20\text{ div/V}
Division gives R = \frac{5000}{20}
Value is 250\text{ }\Omega → (A)

22109:
Loop top needs centripetal balance v^{2} = gR with R = \frac{D}{2}
Energy from release height h gives mgh = mgD + \frac{1}{2}mv^{2}
Inserting v^{2} = \frac{gD}{2} adds \frac{mgD}{4} to mgD
Total becomes mgh = \frac{5mgD}{4}
Cancelling mg gives h = \frac{5}{4}D → (D)

22111:
Momentum along the line of impact is conserved with target initially at rest
Initial value is mv and final is 4mv_2 since the lighter block stops
Equating the two momenta gives v_2 = \frac{v}{4}
Restitution is e = \frac{v_2 - 0}{v - 0}
Ratio equals 0.25 → (B)

22113:
Field force gives a = 6\text{ m s}^{-2} from 0 to 6\text{ m/s} in 1\text{ s}
First second covers s_1 = \frac{1}{2} \times 6 \times 1 = 3\text{ m}
Reversed field sends car forward 3\text{ m} more then back 3\text{ m} by 3\text{ s}
Displacement is 3\text{ m} over 3\text{ s} so mean velocity is 1\text{ m/s}
Path is 9\text{ m} over 3\text{ s} so mean speed is 3\text{ m/s} → (B)

22115:
Radius from moment center is \vec{r} = 0\hat{i} + 2\hat{j} - 1\hat{k}
Force vector is \vec{F} = 4\hat{i} + 5\hat{j} - 6\hat{k}
Moment is \vec{M} = \vec{r} \times \vec{F} evaluated by determinant
Components come out M_x = -7 with M_y = -4 and M_z = -8
Result is -7\hat{i} - 4\hat{j} - 8\hat{k} → (D)

22120:
Rolling gives v = R \omega with K_{t} = \frac{1}{2} m v^{2}
Sphere has I = \frac{2}{5} m R^{2} so K_{r} = \frac{1}{2} I \omega^{2} = \frac{1}{5} m v^{2}
Total is \frac{7}{10} m v^{2} against K_{t} = \frac{1}{2} m v^{2}
Ratio K_{t} : total = 5 : 7, which is option B
→ (B)

22121:
At terminal speed drag balances effective weight and heat rate is F v_{T}
Stokes drag gives F \propto r v_{T} for the small sphere
Terminal speed from the weight balance scales as v_{T} \propto r^{2}
Product scaling gives r^{5}, which is option A
→ (A)

22122:
Wien law keeps \lambda_{m} T fixed so the peak shift scales T by \frac{4}{3}
Stefan law gives black-body power P \propto T^{4}
Power ratio is n = \left(\frac{4}{3}\right)^{4} = \frac{256}{81}
That value is option D
→ (D)

22123:
Equal volumes give A_{1} l_{1} = A_{2} l_{2} with A_{2} = 3 A_{1}
Hence the second wire is shorter with l_{2} = \frac{l_{1}}{3}
Extension \Delta l = \frac{F l}{A Y} at fixed Y then gives F_{2} = 9 F
That force is option C
