22136:
Concentrated \text{H}_{2}\text{SO}_{4} dehydrates formic acid to \text{CO} and oxalic acid to \text{CO} + \text{CO}_{2}
Moles of formic acid equal \frac{2.3}{46} = 0.05 and oxalic acid equal \frac{4.5}{90} = 0.05
\text{KOH} pellets absorb the acidic \text{CO}_{2} fraction and leave the remainder
Remaining CO is 0.05 + 0.05 = 0.1\text{ mol} = 2.8\text{ g}
This matches option A
