22140:
C_{7}H_{8} is toluene \text{C}_{6}\text{H}_{5}\text{CH}_{3}
Side-chain chlorination with excess \text{Cl}_{2} replaces every benzylic H and gives benzotrichloride \text{C}_{6}\text{H}_{5}\text{CCl}_{3}
The \text{CCl}_{3} group is deactivating and meta-directing, so \text{Br}_{2}/\text{Fe} brominates the ring meta to it and gives the m-bromo derivative
Zn/HCl reduces the \text{CCl}_{3} group back to \text{CH}_{3} while the ring bromine survives
Product C is therefore m-bromotoluene
→ (C)

22153:
Mixture c uses 0.2\text{ M} for both acid and base
Moles acid = 75 \times 0.2 = 15\text{ mmol} and base = 25 \times 0.2 = 5\text{ mmol}
Excess \text{H}^{+} = 10\text{ mmol} in 100\text{ mL} gives [\text{H}^{+}] = 0.1\text{ M}
Hence \text{pH} = -\log(0.1) = 1 for mixture c alone, which is option D
→ (D)

22156:
Solubility equilibrium gives K_{\text{sp}} = s^2 with s the molar solubility
Molar s = \frac{2.42 \times 10^{-3}}{233} \approx 1.04 \times 10^{-5}\text{ mol L}^{-1}
Squaring gives K_{\text{sp}} \approx (1.04 \times 10^{-5})^2 \approx 1.08 \times 10^{-10}\text{ mol}^2\text{ L}^{-2}
That value is option C
→ (C)

22159:
Ionic character of hydrides follows Fajans rules with polarizing power of the cation controlling covalency
Smaller highly charging \text{Be}^{2+} polarizes \text{H}^{-} most strongly, giving maximum covalent character to \text{BeH}_{2}
Cation size grows down the group, so polarizing power falls in the order \text{Be}^{2+} > \text{Ca}^{2+} > \text{Ba}^{2+}
Thus ionic character rises as \text{BeH}_{2} < \text{CaH}_{2} < \text{BaH}_{2} → (C)

22161:
Half reactions are \text{MnO}_{4}^{-} + 8\text{H}^{+} + 5e^{-} \rightarrow \text{Mn}^{2+} + 4\text{H}_{2}\text{O} and \text{C}_{2}\text{O}_{4}^{2-} \rightarrow 2\text{CO}_{2} + 2e^{-}
Equalizing electrons requires 2 permanganate gaining 10e^{-} and 5 oxalate releasing 10e^{-}
Balancing O and H then fixes 16\text{H}^{+} and 8\text{H}_{2}\text{O} on respective sides
Thus coefficients are \text{MnO}_{4}^{-}: 2, \text{C}_{2}\text{O}_{4}^{2-}: 5, \text{H}^{+}: 16 → (B)
